  "title": "83: al-Motaffefeen المطففين",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَيْلٌ لِّلْمُطَفِّفِيْنَۙ‏(1)\nWAYLUL LIL-MOTAFFEFEENAL.\nWoe to the defrauders, who use short measures,\nالَّذِيْنَ اِذَا اكْتَالُوْا عَلَى النَّاسِ يَسْتَوْفُوْنَۖ‏(2)\nLAZEENA EZAK TAALOO A’LAN NAASE YASTAWFOON.\nwho, when they measure [a commodity bought] from the people, take the full measure,\nوَاِذَا كَالُوْهُمْ اَوْ وَّزَنُوْهُمْ يُخْسِرُوْنَؕ‏(3)\nWA EZAA KAALOOHUM AW-WAZANOOHUM YUKHSEROON.\nbut diminish when they measure or weigh for them.\nاَلَا يَظُنُّ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَنَّهُمْ مَّبْعُوْثُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nALAA YAZUNNO OOLAAA-EKA ANNAHUM MAB-O’OSOONA.\nDo they not know that they will be resurrected\nلِيَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍۙ‏(5)\nLE-YAWMIN A’ZEEMINY.\non a tremendous day,\nيَّوْمَ يَقُوْمُ النَّاسُ لِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(6)\nYAWMA YAQOOMUN NAASO LE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\na day when mankind will stand before the Lord of all the worlds?\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّ كِتٰبَ الْفُجَّارِ لَفِىْ سِجِّيْنٍؕ‏(7)\nKALLAA INNA KETAABAL FUJJAARE LAFEE SIJJEEEN.\nIndeed, the record of the vicious is in Sijjeen.\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا سِجِّيْنٌؕ‏(8)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA SIJJEEN.\nAnd what will show you what is Sijjeen?\nكِتٰبٌ مَّرْقُوْمٌؕ‏(9)\nKETAABUM MARQOOM.\nIt is a written record.\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَۙ‏(10)\nWAYLUNY YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe to the deniers on that day,\nالَّذِيْنَ يُكَذِّبُوْنَ بِيَوْمِ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(11)\nLAZEENA YOKAZZEBOONA BE-YAWMID DEEN.\nwho deny the Day of Retribution;\nوَمَا يُكَذِّبُ بِهٖۤ اِلَّا كُلُّ مُعْتَدٍ اَثِيْمٍۙ‏(12)\nWA MAA YOKAZZEBOKA BEHI ILLAA KULLO MO’TADIN ASEEM.\nand none denies it except every sinful transgressor.\nاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِ اٰيٰتُنَا قَالَ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَؕ‏(13)\nEZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHE AAYAATONAA QAALA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nWhen Our signs are recited to him, he says, ‘Myths of the ancients!’\nكَلَّا‌ بَلْ رَانَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(14)\nKALLAA BAL, RAANA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nNo, that is not the case! Rather, their hearts have been sullied by what they have been earning.\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّهُمْ عَنْ رَّبِّهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ لَّمَحْجُوْبُوْنَ‌ؕ‏(15)\nKALLAAA INNAHUM A’R RABBEHIM YAWMAEZIL LA-MAHJOOBOON.\nIndeed, they will be alienated from their Lord on that day.\nثُمَّ اِنَّهُمْ لَصَالُوا الْجَحِيْمِؕ‏(16)\nSUMMA INNAHUM LA-SAALUL JAHEEM.\nAfterward they will enter hell,\nثُمَّ يُقَالُ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَؕ‏(17)\nSUMMA YOQAALO HAAZAL LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\nthen told, ‘This is what you used to deny!’\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّ كِتٰبَ الْاَبْرَارِ لَفِىْ عِلِّيِّيْنَؕ‏(18)\nKALLAAA INNA KETAABAL ABRAARE LAFEE I’LLIYYEEN.\nIndeed, the record of the pious is in Illeeyun.\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا عِلِّيُّوْنَؕ‏(19)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA I’LLIYYOON.\nAnd what will show you what is Illeeyun?\nكِتٰبٌ مَّرْقُوْمٌۙ‏(20)\nKETAABUM MARQOOMUN-Y.\nIt is a written record,\nيَّشْهَدُهُ الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَؕ‏(21)\nYASHADOHUL MOQARRABOON.\nwitnessed by those brought near [to Allah].\nاِنَّ الْاَبْرَارَ لَفِىْ نَعِيْمٍۙ‏(22)\nINNAL ABRAARA LAFEE NA-E’EMIN.\nThe pious shall be amid bliss,\nعَلَى الْاَرَآئِكِ يَنْظُرُوْنَۙ‏(23)\nA’LAL ARAAA-EKE YANZOROONA.\nobserving, [as they recline] on couches.\nتَعْرِفُ فِىْ وُجُوْهِهِمْ نَضْرَةَ النَّعِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(24)\nTA’REFO FEE WOJOOHEHIM NAZRATAN NA-E’EM.\nYou will perceive in their faces the freshness of bliss.\nيُسْقَوْنَ مِنْ رَّحِيْقٍ مَّخْتُوْمٍۙ‏(25)\nYUSQAWNA MIR RAHEEQIM MAKHTOOMIN.\nThey will be served with a sealed pure wine,\nخِتٰمُهٗ مِسْكٌ ‌ؕ وَفِىْ ذٰلِكَ فَلْيَتَنَافَسِ الْمُتَنَافِسُوْنَ‏(26)\nKHETAAMOHU MISK, WA FEE ZAALEKA FAL-YATANAAFASIL MOTANAAFESOON.\nwhose seal is musk—for such let the viers vie—\nوَ مِزَاجُهٗ مِنْ تَسْنِيْمٍۙ‏(27)\nWA ME-ZAAJOHU MIN TASNEEMIN.\nand whose seasoning is from Tasneem,\nعَيْنًا يَّشْرَبُ بِهَا الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَؕ‏(28)\nA’YNANY YASHRABO BEHAL MOQARRABOON.\na spring where those brought near [to Allah] drink.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اَجْرَمُوْا كَانُوْا مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يَضْحَكُوْنَ ۖ‏(29)\nINNAL LAZEENA AJRAMOO KAANOO MENAL LAZEENA AAMANOO YAZHAKOON.\nIndeed the guilty used to laugh at the faithful,\nوَاِذَا مَرُّوْا بِهِمْ يَتَغَامَزُوْنَ ۖ‏(30)\nWA EZAA MARROO BEHIM YATAGHAAMAZOON.\nand when they passed them by they would wink at each other,\nوَاِذَا انْقَلَبُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهِمُ انْقَلَبُوْا فَكِهِيْنَ ۖ‏(31)\nWA EZAN QALABOO ELAA AHLEHEMUN QALABOO FAKEHEEN.\nand when they returned to their folks they would return amused,\nوَاِذَا رَاَوْهُمْ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ لَضَآلُّوْنَۙ‏(32)\nWA EZAA RA-AWHUM QAALOO INNA HAA-OOLAAA-E LA-ZAAAL-LOONA.\nand when they saw them they would say, ‘Indeed those are the astray!’\nوَمَاۤ اُرْسِلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ حٰفِظِيْنَۙ‏(33)\nWA MAA URSELOO A’LAYHIM HAAFEZEEN.\nThough they were not sent to watch over them.\nفَالْيَوْمَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنَ الْكُفَّارِ يَضْحَكُوْنَۙ‏(34)\nFAL-YAWMAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MENAL KUFFAARE YAZHAKOONA.\nSo today the faithful will laugh at the faithless,\nعَلَى الْاَرَآئِكِۙ يَنْظُرُوْنَؕ‏(35)\nA’LAL ARAAA-EKE, YANZOROON.\nobserving from their couches:\nهَلْ ثُوِّبَ الْكُفَّارُ مَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(36)\nHAL SUWWEBAL KUFFAARO MAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nHave the faithless been requited for what they used to do?",
  "merits": "Surah al-Motaffefeen (The Defrauders)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 36 verses. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if a person recites this Surah in his obligatory prayers, he will be safe from Hell. He will not even see it, hear it or even come close to it. His accounts for deeds will not be taken.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that if this Surah is recited on a treasure, it will remain safe. In fact, reciting it on anything keeps it safe, even from the vermin of the Earth."
